{"id":"h011","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? The Rosetta Stone is held in the Louvre.","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"The Rosetta Stone is held by the British Museum in London.","confidence":0.99,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":-3.1414},{"text":"The stone has been in the British Museum since 1802.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1414},{"text":"The Louvre has one of the world's great collections of Egyptian antiquities.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.2,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"It is easy to conflate the Louvre and the British Museum.","confidence":0.7,"lean":0.2,"theta":1.0996,"phi":-3.1377},{"text":"The stone is often discussed alongside French Egyptology because Champollion used it to decipher hieroglyphs in the 1820s.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.2,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The stone was surrendered to Britain under the 1801 Capitulation of Alexandria after the French army was defeated.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1414},{"text":"The stone has been on display at the British Museum continuously, catalogued as EA 24.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1414},{"text":"Egypt has long requested the stone's return, yet it remains in London.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.7,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1414},{"text":"The Rosetta Stone is not held in the Louvre, so the claim is false.","confidence":0.99,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":-3.1412}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":8,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},